- 2026-06-10 | **Alpha "constantly compacting" -- Claude Code changed its transcript compact marker (isCompactSummary -> compact_boundary), breaking every byte-based ctx estimator (slot:alpha)** | observed-in: cad-fusion-live-ms0 (this commit) | root cause: current Claude Code marks a compaction with `{"type":"system","subtype":"compact_boundary","compactMetadata":{"preTokens":...}}`, NOT the legacy `"isCompactSummary":true` flag (verified: a 158MB session = `compact_boundary` x13, ZERO `isCompactSummary`-flagged entries). `precompact-auto-trigger.mjs` (tier-T0, PreToolUse) `findLastCompactOffset()`, the shared `transcript-token-counter.mjs`, statusline, the sidecar, and chat-token-watch ALL scanned ONLY the dead legacy flag -> found no boundary -> `estimateFromBytes` counted the WHOLE appended transcript (the JSONL is appended on /compact, never truncated). At 3.5 B/tok a 3.29-3.85MB transcript byte-estimates into the UNGUARDED [HARD=940K, 1.1xCAP=1.1M] band (the >1.1xcap "TOKEN_COUNT_SUSPECT" suppress added 2026-05-21 only catches >1.1M) -> `decision:block` every tool call -> model runs /precompact -> /compact -> file only grows, boundary still unseen -> next tool call blocks again -> constant-compaction loop. Alpha worst-hit (heaviest-injection slot = biggest/fastest-growing transcript + auto-resume reloads it). 2nd path: `lastAssistantTokens` read a pre-compact ~950K turn as authoritative right after a high-watermark compact. The token-awareness sidecar MASKED it (reads authoritative per-turn `usage` = live 345K GREEN); the byte path only fires when the sidecar is stale (>180s, routine on >3min turns under fleet load) + lastAssistantTokens null. fix: centralized `COMPACT_MARKERS` (current+legacy) + pure `lastCompactMarkerOffset` in `transcript-token-counter.mjs`; `findLastCompactOffset` regex + `lastAssistantTokens` boundary-break in the hook; propagated to the 3 inline byte-slice consumers (sidecar/statusline/chat-token-watch); de-duped the redundant `--post` PostToolUse wiring (PreToolUse-only per the hook header, sidecar refresh kept). Real BYTE-PATH + ASSISTANT-PATH regression tests (FAIL pre-fix: "CONTEXT AT 962,327 TOKENS" / "950,000 TOKENS"). counter 48/48 + hook 16/16 + watch 39/39; 2-reviewer per-file PASS. Lessons: centralize harness-format markers (1 edit not N); a byte estimate must never actuate /compact in an unguarded band; compaction appends-never-shrinks so estimators MUST be boundary-aware; in the shared `H:/prism` tree `git stash` is GLOBAL (collides with peer stashes) -- never use for test isolation. | verify: `git -C H:/prism show <this>` · [[compact-boundary-format-change-constant-compaction]] · [[reference_compact_boundary_format_fix_2026_06_10]]
- 2026-06-11 | **GNN self-retrain lifecycle OOM'd on its in-process graph load -- only the spawned TRAINER had a heap bump (slot:charlie)** | observed-in: 8d6a481080 + 15123dff67 (+ HEAP-FIX-3 helper/execArgv) | root cause: surfaced validating U-AISYN-GNN-NODEFEAT (the 34 galaxy node-features I'd merged into india's `node-embeddings-768d.jsonl`). `nn-graph-retrain-lifecycle.mjs --force` crashed with a JS heap OOM at ~381MB, 2.5s in -- BEFORE training. The trainer SUBPROCESS got `--max-old-space-size=8192` (line ~288) but the lifecycle's OWN node process runs the eval (`runAssessment`) + base-embedding builds IN-PROCESS, each loading the ~550MB system graph, with the DEFAULT heap. A sibling OOM (exit 134/SIGABRT) hit the step-2c galaxy-embedding child (`build-galaxy-node-embeddings.mjs`), spawned WITHOUT the flag too -- fail-soft, so the retrain silently continued on the PRIOR run's galaxy features. fix: pure `shouldReexecForHeap(argv,env,execArgv)` + a `__isMain` self-reexec that re-launches node once with `--max-old-space-size` (`PRISM_NN_RETRAIN_LIFECYCLE_HEAP_MB`, default 8192; cheap `--status`/`--help` skip; `PRISM_NN_RETRAIN_REEXEC=1` breaks the loop; `hasHeapFlag(process.execArgv)` skips a redundant re-exec when the scheduled task already passed the flag); shared tested `nodeArgsWithHeap()` regression-locks the flag at BOTH spawn sites. VALIDATED: retrain ran to completion (EXIT 0, 0 OOM) -- but AUROC 0.40 on the 6000-node capped subgraph (macro-F1 0.14 / Brier 0.25), BELOW the 0.78 gate, so correctly NOT promoted; the 34 galaxy node-features add COVERAGE (`hit=6000 miss=0`) but did not lift the gate (consistent with the known link-pred-pretext variance; full-coverage is ref-pool growth, not this fix). 57/57 tests; 3-of-3 PASS. Lesson: when a script spawns a heap-bumped child but ALSO does heavy work in its OWN process, the parent needs the bump too -- a self-reexec fixes every launch path (ad-hoc + scheduled) at once. | verify: `git -C H:/prism show 8d6a481080` · [[reference_ai_systems_6unit_complete_2026_06_11]]
- 2026-06-10 | **HS-01: a BARE `stable-session-id.mjs` call miskeyed handoffs to a PEER chat -> auto-session-start silently broken fleet-wide (slot:alpha)** | observed-in: e81dec5cba (fleet-wide fix) + 7dec157db0 (arg-anchor) | root cause: the `STABLE=$(stable-session-id.mjs)` pattern in /precompact + /handoff + 78 per-slot wrappers passes NO CLI arg and has NO stdin -> `getStableIdentifier()` fell through to the PID-pin heuristic (anchor 2), which with N concurrent chats sharing one cwd returned a PEER chat's id (confirmed live: `claude-c48a1aff` for session db273e77). The handoff was written/read under the wrong key -> the next session's auto-resume could not find it -> auto-session-start was DEAD in production exactly when the fleet was busy. The first fix (7dec157db0) added an explicit `--session-id` anchor (0), but that needs 24+ caller edits to actually use. The REAL fix (e81dec5cba): the harness exports `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` into EVERY tool subprocess's env, scoped to THIS chat's process (a per-process var CANNOT be a peer's id -- subprocess env inheritance is strictly downward; `compact-counter.mjs:14-22` already relies on this exact isolation). One new anchor (1.5) in the single shared helper, ranked ABOVE the PID-pin, fixes every bare caller + hook + wrapper at once with ZERO caller edits -- fleet-wide the instant it commits. The pre-existing env anchor (3) read the WRONG var name (`CLAUDE_SESSION_ID`, UNSET; harness sets `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID`). LIVE PROOF: bare `node stable-session-id.mjs` -> `claude-db273e77` (was a peer); per-agent-handoff read via the bare pattern -> `matchedBy:same-instance-newest`. 10/10 tests, 3-of-3 PASS. Lesson: a per-process env var the harness sets is a more robust multi-chat anchor than any shared-file PID/cwd heuristic, and fixing the shared substrate beats editing N call sites (R7/R8). | verify: `git -C H:/prism show e81dec5cba` · [[reference_hs01_env_anchor_fleetwide_2026_06_10]]
- 2026-06-10 | **Stop-hook handoff-append silently no-ops on a full-uuid sid -- findHandoff matched the wrong key (slot:alpha, surfaced building U-TASK-BOUNDARY-COMPACT)** | observed-in: 9fcda446a1 | root cause: a Stop hook's `f.includes(sid)` handoff matcher is fed `resolveSessionId() = stdin.session_id` = the FULL uuid (`db273e77-fb5e-...`), but per-agent handoffs are keyed by the SHORT chatId (`HANDOFF-claude-db273e77-<topic>.md`). `"HANDOFF-claude-db273e77-...".includes("db273e77-fb5e-...")` = FALSE (verified live) -> the durable handoff append silently never fires in prod. Fixed in the NEW hook (stop-task-boundary-compact-nudge.mjs): resolve the authoritative chatId from chat-slots.json + anchor `HANDOFF-${chatId}-` (also kills the under-anchored substring peer-leak; R9 prod-path test pins it). LATENT IN THE SIBLING `stop-force-loop-continue.mjs::findHandoff` (identical `f.includes(sid)` + full-uuid `resolveSessionId`) -> its `## RESUME_LOOP` auto-continue append is almost certainly also dead in prod; flagged for a scoped follow-up (not fixed here -- R8 separate unit). Also caught pre-ship by R9: the handoff-append regex `m`-flag + leading-`\n*` truncation (replaced only the marker header / jammed `# H## COMPACT_SEAM`). | verify: `git -C H:/prism show 9fcda446a1` · [[reference_task_boundary_compact_nudge_2026_06_10]]
- 2026-06-10 | **documented-by cross-substrate edges silently collapsed 38->0 -- confirmed against a VOLATILE rotating augmentation (slot:sierra)** | observed-in: 88cb72b532 | root cause: `generate-cross-substrate-edges.mjs` confirmed documented-by knowledge-note endpoints against `memNodeIds` = the newNodes of the ROTATING `memories-atomic-augmentation.json` (it emits only a few recent notes). When the `memory_patterns.<galaxy>_synthesis` nodes rotated out, documented-by collapsed to 0 -- even though the system-viz merge is ADD-only so those synthesis nodes still LIVE in the merged graph. The regenerated artifact + its test were ALREADY red ~8h, undetected. fix: confirm knowledge notes against the node-card OFFSET ORACLE (`node-card-offsets.json`, ~336K merged-graph node ids, cheap parse, no 548MB load) instead -- restored documented-by to 320 (42 synthesis@1.0 + 278 backlink@0.9, MORE than the original 38 because the full note set resolves far more authored backlinks) + hardened vs silent re-collapse. Shipped alongside U-XSUB-EMBEDS (3rd typed edge `embeds`: 948 edges = the NN/GNN/RAG 768d embedding footprint surfaced in the search graph). 7/7 tests incl oracle-absent CI path proven; per-file 2-reviewer PASS. Lesson: confirm endpoints against the STABLE ADD-only merged-graph oracle, never a rotating augmentation -- a generator reading a volatile source silently loses coverage when it rotates. | verify: `git -C H:/prism show 88cb72b532` · [[reference_xsub_embeds_docby_oracle_2026_06_10]]
- 2026-06-10 | **Generated session handoff surfaced a PEER's commit as "Last work" (handoff-stub leak, slot:alpha)** | observed-in: be9182dca7 | root cause: `precompact-handoff.mjs::generateSmartResume` built the "Last work" line from `git log --oneline` on the SHARED `cad-fusion-live-ms0` tree -> it surfaced the fleet's most-recent commit, NOT this chat's. Live symptom: a hotel UI commit auto-resumed an alpha verified-offload session (the operator's "handoffs are stubs by helper agents" report). The writer-ban (live-chat-only) was intact; the leak was the GENERATED content. fix: slot-scope the grep to THIS slot's own commits, anchored on the OPENING paren `(slot:<slot>` so a mid-message MENTION of another slot (`(slot:india rescuing slot:papa orphan)`) never false-matches (proven: 0 false-matches for papa, 371 true self-matches for alpha); labeled fleet-commit fallback (R12); + `buildReentryDirective(slot)` ends every synthesized resume with the `/startup-<slot> /loop [10m] /goal` re-entry so no generated handoff is a dead-end. SESSION-CONTINUITY-AGENTIC also auto-starts that sequence on all 3 startup surfaces + gives spawned agents their parent slot's galaxy pack + makes /goal force R15 100%-completion. Lesson: a "Last work" line derived from `git log` on a shared multi-chat tree is a peer-leak unless slot-scoped. | verify: `git -C H:/prism show be9182dca7` · [[reference_session_continuity_agentic_2026_06_10]]
- 2026-06-10 | **SFC radial_depth INERT in prism_optimized + hex_mm force-collapse at full slot (slot:oscar)** | observed-in: 69146aa9c1 | root cause: TWO coupled bugs closing the last SFC axis gap. (1) `SpeedFeedNineAxisOrchestratorEngine.ts` prism_optimized (~895) recomputed `ae = (alt.ae_pct/100)*D` from the balanced ALTERNATIVE's static table, discarding the operator's `toolpath.radial_depth_mm/_pct` -> MRR IDENTICAL 5%->100% engagement (axis fully inert; cost_batch/aggressive_rush already honored `sfc.radial_depth.value`, only prism_optimized broke it). (2) `UltimateSpeedFeedEngine.ts` STEP 9 (~2245) `hex_mm = fz*sin(acos(1-2*ae/Dc))` DECAYED past ae/Dc=0.5 (sin of an angle >90deg) to ~0 at a full slot -> Fc->0 where engagement is GREATEST; since the orchestrator workholding + spindle-power clamps read `sfc.forces`, honoring a high user ae with forces~0 would UNDER-PROTECT (oscar red line). fix: (1) `ae = userGaveRadial(>0) ? sfc.radial_depth.value : table` -- engine resolved it AND computed sfc.forces at the SAME ae, so clamps stay force-consistent with no re-derivation; (2) `hex = immersionRatio>=0.5 ? fz : fz*sin(acos(1-2*immersionRatio))` -- max chip = fz for ae>=Dc/2 (peak at the 90deg centerline; Sandvik/Boothroyd-Knight), byte-identical ae<Dc/2, continuous at Dc/2, SAFE-DIRECTION (forces only increase). +12 R9 tests (all RED pre-fix); 401-gauntlet + variability + orchestrator + all-axis sweep PASS; 3-of-3 + physics-reviewer PASS (mandatory force formula). Lesson: when an orchestrator overrides an engine-resolved value with a static-table proxy, the user input goes inert AND the downstream safety clamps (reading the engine's force at the real ae) silently decouple. P2 follow-ups (pre-existing): negative explicit radial_depth_mm -> engine NaN; max(1,Dc) sub-mm immersion floor. | verify: `git -C H:/prism show 69146aa9c1` · [[reference_oscar_radial_engagement_fix_2026_06_10]]
- 2026-06-10 | **Unwired-engine audit blind to engine->engine consumption -- 23 library engines mis-counted UNWIRED (slot:sierra)** | observed-in: a6dbec1842 | root cause: `scripts/audit-unwired-engines.mjs` (source of BUILD_STATE NEEDS_WIRING + the fleet "N unwired engines" count + /system-viz ghost-orphan roosts) scanned consumers = {dispatchers,routes,registries,orchestrators,hooks,singletons} but NOT plain engine->engine consumption -> a library-layer engine consumed only by other (non-orch/non-singleton) engines (e.g. QdrantVectorStoreEngine, 3 engine-consumers) showed UNWIRED + was chased as a false dispatcher-wiring target (R13 zero-gain churn). fix: extracted a pure exported `applyConsumerClassification` + added a LAST-priority self-excluded WIRED-VIA-ENGINE pass (dispatcher/route/etc still win first-match). LIVE: UNWIRED **89 -> 66 truly-dormant + 23 library-layer** (reconciles exactly); 23/23 tests (5 new). The actionable dormant set is 66, not 89. 3rd audit-detector fix in this file. | verify: `git -C H:/prism show a6dbec1842` · [[reference_audit_wired_via_engine_2026_06_10]]
- 2026-06-10 | **Tribal brain CLOBBER #4 -- shard-transition read-blind dropped 29,723 -> ~11,500 entries (slot:sierra, self-inflicted by running the coverage batch)** | observed-in: 8bf1873577 | root cause: `tribal-embed-index.mjs` readIndex() + writeIndex()'s clobber-guard checked existence via `fs.existsSync(INDEX_PATH)` (MONOLITH .json ONLY). When the index first crossed ~480 MiB it SHARDED (write-tribal-index.mjs writes .manifest.json + shards and retireSupersededArtifacts REMOVES the monolith .json) -> next readIndex saw .json absent -> returned EMPTY base -> buildOrUpdate.persist() merged staged-only -> writeIndex's removeShardLayout DELETED the shards (the 29,723 base lived there). Clobber-guard had the same monolith-only blind spot so it silently did NOT run. Latent since the shard writer shipped after the 2026-06-08 readIndex fail-loud fixes; fired on the first-ever shard transition (which the streaming-rerank heap-ceiling removal enabled). fix: BOTH checks MANIFEST-AWARE (empty/skip ONLY when neither .json NOR .manifest.json exists; loadTribalIndex reads shards). 14/14 incl 2 forced-shard regression tests (fail pre-fix). Brain recoverable (source intact); re-embed restoring. **3 sibling embedders share the vector (dormant-while-monolith): embed-engines/embed-knowledge-store/embed-cited-tips -> follow-up U-TRIBAL-SIBLING-WRITER-SHARD-SAFE (route ALL writers through loadTribalIndex+writeTribalIndex).** Lesson: a new on-disk layout must be reflected in EVERY existence/guard check; don't run a long index-mutating batch on the live brain unattended. | verify: `git -C H:/prism show 8bf1873577` · [[reference_tribal_shard_read_clobber_2026_06_10]]
- 2026-06-09 | **Runout tool-life DOUBLE-COUNT -- engine fix met an obsolete consumer workaround (slot:oscar)** | observed-in: 73b97ef25f | root cause: U-OSC-RUNOUT-LIFE-DERATE (a8f72823cb) made UltimateSpeedFeedEngine fold the runout life reduction into `tool_life.life_minutes`. But SpeedFeedNineAxisOrchestratorEngine had a pre-existing compensating workaround (U-OSC-HOLDER-RUNOUT-LIFE) that read the SAME `runout_impact.life_reduction_pct` and did `life *= keep` -- built because the engine USED to only warn. Once the engine owned the derate, the orchestrator's `life` (= already-derated `sfc.tool_life.life_minutes`) got derated AGAIN -> `tool_life_min` = raw * keep^2 (proven: engineFactor 0.884 single vs orchFactor 0.795 ~ 0.884^2; cost fallback path double-counted too). The engine's OWN isolated 3-of-3 scrutiny could not see the consumer's fork. fix: remove the orchestrator's `life *= keep` (engine is now the single source, R8/R7), keep the operator advisory warning. TDD red->green test `sfc-nine-axis-runout-no-double-count.test.ts` (ratio cancels co-varying derates: orchFactor must match engine SINGLE factor, NOT its square). Lesson: when an engine fix folds an advisory INTO its headline output, grep EVERY consumer for a workaround applying the same term. | verify: `git -C H:/prism show 73b97ef25f` · [[feedback_audit_consumers_when_moving_logic_into_engine]]
- 2026-06-08 | **Fail-OPEN read CLOBBERED the tribal brain 33,639→1 entries (slot:golf)** | observed-in: a3e6d3ca97 | root cause: the V8-cap read-failure (182788232a) had a worse second manifestation. `.claude/scripts/tribal-embed-index.mjs` `readIndex()` had a fail-OPEN `catch` that **returned a fresh empty `{entries:[]}` on any parse error** ("starting fresh"). When the 537MB index threw the cap error, an `--add`/`--update` (auto-embed hook on a wiki Write) loaded the EMPTY base, spliced 1 file, and `writeIndex()`'d it → clobbered the 537MB/33,639-entry brain to a 1-entry 16KB stub (signature: no `wikiEmbeddedAt`, fresh `generatedAt`). 537MB version gitignored → unrecoverable; rename-replace bypassed recycle bin. fix: (1) `readIndex` cap-safe-loads + **FAILS LOUD** when the file exists-but-won't-load (never empty-then-clobber); (2) `writeIndex` **clobber-guard** refuses a >50% shrink over a populated index unless `PRISM_TRIBAL_ALLOW_SHRINK=1` (alone blocks the 33,639→1 write); (3) loader closing-`]` assert (torn-file fail-loud). RESTORED the surviving 4,162-entry baseline (2026-05-20, slot worktrees); lost ~29K delta is re-embeddable. 7/7 guard + 10/10 loader; live rerank + --stats clean. Lesson: a fail-OPEN `catch→return empty` on a re-written corpus is silent-total-destruction; `catch` on an EXISTING file must fail loud. | verify: `git -C H:/prism show a3e6d3ca97` · [[reference_tribal_index_v8_string_cap_2026_06_08]]
- 2026-06-08 | **Tribal index crossed V8's 512MiB string cap → tribal injection (PSN leg #5) silently DEAD fleet-wide (slot:golf)** | observed-in: 182788232a | root cause: `state/shared/tribal-embed-index.json` reached 536,988,127 B, crossing V8's hard max string length `0x1fffffe8`=536,870,888 B by 117KB. Every consumer doing `JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path,"utf8"))` now throws `Cannot create a string longer than 0x1fffffe8 characters` BEFORE parsing — the LIVE `.claude/scripts/tribal-rerank.mjs:76` (PSN leg #5, fires every UserPromptSubmit) returned NOTHING in every chat with no error surfaced; the wiki embedder read was also blocked. `--max-old-space-size` does NOT help (string-length limit, not heap — the earlier 533MB heap-OOM was a different wall). fix: `scripts/lib/load-tribal-index.mjs` reads the index as a Buffer (no string cap) — fast-path JSON.parse under cap (byte-identical), incremental brace-aware entries walker over cap; wired into tribal-rerank + embedder read. 8/8 loader + 23/23 embedder; LIVE 537MB/33,639-entry index read in 3.4s 0-corrupt, rerank returns real mill hits. KNOWN-REMAINING: the WRITE side (`JSON.stringify` of a >cap object) also throws → appending entries needs index **sharding** (next unit). | verify: `git -C H:/prism show 182788232a` · [[reference_tribal_index_v8_string_cap_2026_06_08]]
- 2026-06-08 | **OCR closed-loop read page-0 ONLY of 96%-multi-page drawings + ran to completion on a reaper kill (slot:xray)** | observed-in: b76b4d55ab + 265e8a6e41 | root cause: TWO corpus-scale defects surfaced building "begin closed-loop training on all prints". (1) **page-0-only**: `blueprint-ocr-training-loop.mjs` rasterized PDF page 0 only — but a STEP-2b sample proved **96% of JM drawing PDFs are multi-page (2-32pp)**, so ~76% of dimension-bearing pages were silently dropped (a 4pp print contributed 1 page's dims, not 4). (2) **non-resumable corpus burn**: the runner held every print in memory + `writeFileSync` ONCE at the end → a fleet-reaper kill at print N/M (host reaps long node/python under load) lost ALL N and restarted at print 1 — a non-terminating GPU burn that LOOKS like progress. fix: `rasterizePrintPages` renders ALL pages (cap 12, `capped` logged) + per-page ensemble → one (page-image,dims) pair per page; per-print stream-append to trainset/queue/`processed-cursor.jsonl` (durable rows BEFORE cursor) + `parseCursorDoneSet`/`partitionByResumeCursor` resume (re-OCR=0). Real denominator: `build-print-corpus-manifest.mjs` SEARCHES juliett's documents.jsonl → 7794 drawing prints (not 257K, not a toy set), 76978 business excluded. LIVE: RUN1 OCR'd 2 PDFs, RUN2 resume re-OCR=0 (1s vs 42s); a 4pp print → 4 per-page rows / 7 gold dims. 31/31 tests; per-file 2-reviewer fixed run-as-main-guard×3 + downstream key+page last-wins dedup. | verify: `git -C H:/prism show 265e8a6e41` · [[reference_xray_ocr_corpus_resumable_multipage_2026_06_08]]
- 2026-06-06 | **OCR closed-loop lost EVERY print's extraction over one malformed number — truncation×leading-dot + leading-`+` (slot:xray)** | observed-in: e354869c93 | root cause: the multi-VLM ensemble reported "0 models survived / all-failed" on every print (incl. extrude_punch.png which made gold labels 06-04). The VLM extracts fine; the loss is at `parseVisionResponse` (`scripts/lib/ollama-vision-extract-lib.mjs`): (1) a truncated response (unterminated trailing string) makes `repairLeadingDotDecimals` BAIL (fail-safe return) → an earlier value-position `.86` survives → `repairTruncatedJson` closes the braces but NOT the notation → JSON.parse fails → whole extraction discarded; (2) VLMs emit `+0.015` for a `±` tolerance — JSON allows leading `-` but never leading `+`. Stochastic VLM output → intermittent total-loss. fix: repairTruncatedJson closes the unterminated trailing string (+drops a dangling escape); fallback parse paths re-apply repairLeadingDotDecimals AFTER truncation repair (structure-first, then notation); repairLeadingDotDecimals also strips a value-position leading `+` (exponents + string interiors preserved). 61/61 tests (7 new, R9-verified by revert); LIVE same print now extracts 8-9 dims → 7/9 trainable, calibration 0→38. Per-file 2-reviewer PASS (1 P1 dangling-escape fixed). THE blocker to corpus closed-loop training — not the VLM or GPU. | verify: `git -C H:/prism show e354869c93` · [[reference_xray_ocr_parse_truncation_fix_2026_06_06]]
- 2026-06-04 | **VLM OCR silently discarded a WHOLE print over one leading-dot decimal `.171` (slot:xray)** | observed-in: cad-fusion-live-ms0 (uncommitted) | root cause: vision models emit engineering notation `"nominal": .171` (no leading zero) — valid manufacturing shorthand, INVALID JSON — so `parseVisionResponse` (`scripts/lib/ollama-vision-extract-lib.mjs`) threw on JSON.parse and lost the ENTIRE extraction (a full print of dims over one number; same silent-data-loss class as the truncation bug `repairTruncatedJson` already guards). Surfaced live during the multi-VLM ensemble build: qwen2.5vl:7b OCR'd a `.171"` dim → 0 dims extracted. fix: sanitizer `jsonText.replace(/([:,\[])(\s*)(-?)\.(\d)/g, "$1$2$30.$4")` inserts the zero ONLY in a JSON value position (after `:`/`,`/`[`, optional ws+sign) so a quoted string value (`: ".005"`) or string interior (`"dim .250 ref"`) is never touched. +2 regression tests (54/54). Live re-run: `.171"` recovered as 4.3434mm, F1 0.8 vs truth. Shipped alongside `vision-ensemble-fuse.mjs` (multi-VLM consensus OCR — Blackwell unlock: N diverse families resident+concurrent, ≥2-agree=corroborated, 1-of-N=hallucination-candidate). | verify: `rtk node --test scripts/lib/ollama-vision-extract-lib.test.mjs` · [[vlm-ensemble-ocr-and-leading-dot-parse-fix]]
- 2026-06-03 | **NN/GNN schema-read blindness, one shape deeper — `classifyGnn` blind to the GRADED NN-EVAL shape (slot:india)** | observed-in: 93f85ec067 | root cause: U-NN-REFPOOL-REEVAL re-ran `nn-graph-eval` against today's live 676MB graph; the perma-DEFERRED eval (poolSize 0, stale May-16) finally produced a real **62-ghost holdout** → the GRADED shape `{deferred:false, metrics:{auroc,brier}, grade:{verdict}}` with NO `checkpointMeta`/`checkpointPresent`. But `classifyGnn` (the canonical reader the f436b2c614 fix routed BOTH consumers through) read AUROC *only* from `checkpointMeta.auroc` → graded report classified `{dormant:true, auroc:null}` → both fleet hooks (psn-leg-state per-prompt ×26 slots + nn-graph-health SessionStart) newly mis-reported a real measured grade as "DORMANT poolSize 0 / AUROC n/a". Same regression CLASS as f436b2c614, exposed because the producer's second output shape was never exercised while the eval was data-blocked. fix: classifyGnn reads `metrics.auroc/brier` (deploy gate) first, falls back to `checkpointMeta` (link-pred pretext), treats a scored holdout as checkpoint-present so a graded report is never dormant — only below-gate/healthy. Leg #10 now honestly = AUROC 0.5 (8-dim classifier collapsed to a constant `prism_turning` predictor) BELOW-GATE. +9 tests (87 total green), 2-reviewer PASS 0 P0/P1. | verify: `git -C H:/prism show 93f85ec067` · [[nn-graded-schema-read-fix]]
- 2026-06-02 | **WEDM tech-tables registry lost 2 of 5 ACU 7-pass E-code families (E952/E56xx) + getJMDiePatternForMaterial silently mislabeled compound materials (slot:mike)** | observed-in: cad-fusion-live-ms0 (uncommitted) | root cause: `JM_DIE_ECODE_FAMILIES` + `selectECodeFamily` were never wired to the real extracted FA-S data (`mitsubishi-fa-s-extracted.ts`) → `wedm-acu-7pass.test.ts` RED (17/20), `WEDMProgramOptimizerEngine.find(f.id.includes("acu"))`→undefined, neural-analysis family lookup missed; meanwhile a THIRD selector `WireEDMDeepAIHardeningEngine._selectECodeFamily` had its own acu impl (R7 N-divergent-selectors drift). Separately `getJMDiePatternForMaterial` returned a confident `standard_4pass` for uncalibrated compound/exotic materials (carbide/Inconel/Ti/17-4PH/CPM), poisoning `WEDMNeuralTrainingEngine:2109` labels. fix: `buildAcuFamilyFromFAS()` single-sources E952/E56xx from extracted records (3→5 families) + ACU branch in `selectECodeFamily` + `material_calibrated`/`warning` fail-loud flag (calibrated set single-sourced from the registry). RED→GREEN, 117/117. | verify: `node mcp-server/scripts/wedm-print-to-program-accuracy.ts` · [[reference_acu_7pass_families_regression_2026_06_02]]
- 2026-06-02 | **NN/GNN PSN-leg health fabricated an "embeddingSource mismatch" diagnosis fleet-wide — schema-read blindness (slot:india)** | observed-in: f436b2c614 | root cause: `psn-leg-state-inject.legStateNnGraph` read top-level `evalDoc.auroc`, but real `NN-EVAL.json` nests it at `checkpointMeta.auroc` + carries `deferred`/`reason`/`poolSize` → read ALWAYS undefined → every prompt across all 26 slots emitted "AUROC not finite … likely embeddingSource mismatch" (a fabricated cause; true state = DEFERRED, insufficient-reference-pool poolSize 0, AUROC 0.096). India's own "schema-read-blindness" regression class — two consumers of one state file diverged (nn-graph-health-inject read it correctly via `classifyGnn`). fix: delegate read to canonical `classifyGnn` (one source of truth) + type-strict top-level fallback (guards `Number(null)===0`) + `DEFERRED` status w/ real reason + gate on `classifyGnn.healthy` (AUROC *and* Brier, fail-closed) + export `PROMOTE_AUROC_MIN`/`PROMOTE_BRIER_MAX` (no re-inlined 0.78). 81/81 tests incl real-data anti-drift + negative-assert the fabricated string can't return. Also verified `U-NN-TRAINER-EXPORT-RESTORE` is a STALE CLAUDE.md claim (exports present, 154/154 pass). | verify: `git -C H:/prism show f436b2c614` · [[nn-leg-schema-read-fix]]
- 2026-06-01 | **fleet-task-health watched only 12/39 PRISM scheduled tasks — `discoverInstallerTasks` blind in 2 dims (slot:bravo)** | observed-in: 213a1da6f8 | root cause: KNOWN list synced to its OWN blind discovery (typed-param-only regex + `install-*-task.ps1`-singular glob; spec-key `Name=` + `-tasks/-cron/register-*` registrars unseen) → drift test self-referentially green-but-blind; 27 safety-net tasks silently unwatched. fix: complete-by-construction — `Register-ScheduledTask` content gate + broad glob + 3 capture forms; KNOWN 12→39; +Zulu Orchestrator CRASH_CRITICAL. 52/52 tests, per-file scrutiny A+B PASS (B caught 2 layers). | verify: `git -C H:/prism show 213a1da6f8` · [[fleet-task-health-discovery-drift]]
